# Terraform working state, written by `terraform init` in the module and the
# installation example. Same reasoning as acceptance/gcp/.gitignore: the plugin
# cache is machine-local and large, and a lock file pins provider hashes for the
# platform that ran init. The gate never uses either -- check.sh initializes a
# disposable copy of this tree -- so a committed lock would churn per operator
# while pinning nothing the gate actually reads.
**/.terraform/
**/.terraform.lock.hcl
